&=\frac{1}{4}x & \text{Reciprocate and cross multiply}
\end{align*}

*Second Term:*
\begin{align*}
\left( \frac{3x^3}{x} \right)^2 &= \frac{\left( 3x^3 \right)^2}{\left( x \right)^2} & \text{Using the property}~\left( \frac{a}{b} \right)^n=\frac{a^n}{b^n}\\\\
&= \frac{9x^{6}}{x^{2}} & \text{Simplify}\left( 3x^3 \right)^2 = 9x^6\text{ and} \left( x \right)^2 =x^2
