<answer>Hence by pattern observation we see that the $n$th term will always be a power of $1,2,$ or $4$. The last digit remains cycle($f(n)$) every $5$ terms.
$$f(n)=\begin{cases}
1, & \begin{array}{}
2 \mod 5 == 0 \\
\end{array}\\
2, & \begin{array}{}
2 \mod 5 == 1\\
\end{array} \\
1, & \begin{array}{}
2 \mod 5 == 2\\
\end{array}\\
4, & \begin{array}{}
2 \mod 5 == 3\\
\end{array}\\
2, & \begin{array}{}
