\begin{eqnarray*}
\begin{pmatrix} 5 \\ -12 \end{pmatrix} &=& \begin{pmatrix} \cos \theta & -\sin \theta \\ \sin \theta & \cos \theta \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 13 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix} \\
&=& \begin{pmatrix} 13 \cos \theta \\ 13 \sin \theta \end{pmatrix}.
\end{eqnarray*}
Thus, $13 \cos \theta = 5$ and $13 \sin \theta = -12.$ Solving, we find that $\cos \theta = \frac{5}{13}$ and $\sin \theta = -\frac{12}{13}.$<end think>
